{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14263949,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":6,"pointsAwarded":6,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57975,"firstName":"Harrison","lastName":"Charles","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO3yHD4gcTFRx97dYjQXmX1","sequenceId":19},"course":{"id":111,"name":"Mathematical Foundations II"},"topic":{"id":1361,"name":"Integrating the Reciprocal Function"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T10:52:59.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T10:57:23.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T10:58:11.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T10:58:31.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62366010,"created":"2026-10-16T10:57:37.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14487,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 10:57 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":29886,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":375,"text":"<p>Find the integral of $2x^{7/3} - \\dfrac{1}{3x}$ with respect to $x.$ </p>\n","choice1":"$\\dfrac{3}{5} x^{10/3} - \\dfrac 1 3\\ln |x|+C$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{7}{5} x^{7/3} - 3\\ln |x|+C$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{1}{5} x^{1/3} -\\dfrac 1 3\\ln |x|+C$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{7}{2} x^{2/3} - \\ln |x|+C$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{5}{2} x^{7/3} -3\\ln |x|+C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int \\left( 2x^{7/3} - \\dfrac{1}{3x} \\right)  \\textrm{d}x&=\n\\int 2x^{7/3} \\, \\textrm{d}x - \\dfrac 1 3\\int\\dfrac{1}{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\[3pt]\n&=2\\cdot\\dfrac{x^{7/3+1}}{\\left(\\dfrac{7}{3}+1\\right)} - \\dfrac 1 3\\ln |x| +C\\\\\n&=\\dfrac{3}{5} x^{10/3} - \\dfrac 1 3\\ln |x|+C.\n\n\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":1361,"name":"Integrating the Reciprocal Function"},"example":{"id":375,"title":"Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function"},"group":{"id":97385,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263949,"answer":{"id":62366010,"cread":"2026-10-16T10:57:37.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14487},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62366026,"created":"2026-10-16T10:57:53.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12946,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 10:57 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":49067,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":376,"text":"<p>What is the antiderivative of $ \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{x} \\right)^2?$</p>\n","choice1":"$x- \\dfrac{1}{x}+2 \\ln(K|x|)$","choice2":"$x- \\dfrac{1}{x}+ \\ln(2K|x|)$","choice3":"$1- \\dfrac{1}{x}+2 \\ln(|K|x)$","choice4":"$x+\\Big(1+\\ln(K|x|)\\Big)^2$","choice5":"$1+2 \\ln(|K|x)$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Expanding the binomial and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\int \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{x} \\right)^2\\textrm{d} x\n\t&= \\int \\left(1+\\dfrac{2}{x}+ \\dfrac{1}{x^2} \\right)\\textrm{d} x\\\\[3pt]\n&= \\int \\textrm{d} x+ 2 \\int \\dfrac{1}{x}\\,\\textrm{d} x+ \\int \\dfrac{1}{x^2}\\,\\textrm{d} x\\\\[3pt]\n\t&=x+2\\ln|x| + \\dfrac{x^{-2+1}}{-2+1} + C\\\\[3pt]\n&=x+2\\ln|x| - \\dfrac{1}{x} + C.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Lastly, let&#39;s rewrite the constant so that we can combine it with the natural logarithm. For any constant $C,$ we can always write $C =2\\ln{K}$ where $K$ is some other positive constant. Doing this allows us to combine the constant with $2\\ln|x|$ term, and we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\int \\left(1+\\dfrac{1}{x} \\right)^2\\textrm{d} x\n\t&=x- \\dfrac{1}{x} + 2\\ln|x| + 2\\ln{K}\\\\[3pt]\n\t&=x- \\dfrac{1}{x}+2\\left(\\ln|x| + \\ln{K}\\right)\\\\[3pt]\n\t&=x- \\dfrac{1}{x}+2 \\ln(K|x|).\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":1361,"name":"Integrating the Reciprocal Function"},"example":{"id":376,"title":"Integrating a Reciprocal Function and Simplifying the Arbitrary Constant Using the Laws of Logarithms"},"group":{"id":52311,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263949,"answer":{"id":62366026,"cread":"2026-10-16T10:57:53.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12946},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62366094,"created":"2026-10-16T10:58:11.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14082,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 10:58 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":103373,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":375,"text":"<p>Find the integral of $\\dfrac{2}{x}+3x^{2}$ with respect to $x.$</p>\n","choice1":"$2\\ln |x| + x^3 + C$","choice2":"$3\\ln |x| + 3x^3 + C$","choice3":"$3\\ln |x| + 2x^3 + C$","choice4":"$\\ln |x| + x^3 + C$","choice5":"$2\\ln |x| + 3x^2 + C$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int \\left( \\dfrac{2}{x}+3x^{2} \\right)  \\textrm{d}x\n&= 2\\int \\dfrac1x \\, \\textrm{d}x +3 \\int x^2 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\[3pt]\n&= 2\\ln |x| + x^3 + C.\n\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":1361,"name":"Integrating the Reciprocal Function"},"example":{"id":375,"title":"Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function"},"group":{"id":97385,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14263949,"answer":{"id":62366094,"cread":"2026-10-16T10:58:11.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14082},"graphic":false,"d